DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The  mmaalllloocc__iinnffoo()  function  exports  an XML string that describes the
       current state of the memory‐allocation implementation  in  the  caller.
       The  string  is printed on the file stream _s_t_r_e_a_m.  The exported string
       includes information about all arenas (see mmaalllloocc(3)).

       As currently implemented, _o_p_t_i_o_n_s must be zero.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       On success, mmaalllloocc__iinnffoo() returns 0.  On failure, it  returns  -1,  and
       _e_r_r_n_o is set to indicate the error.

